h therefore contributes $(-v^{-1})q^{-(s-1)}(v-v^{-1}\delta)=q^{-s}\delta-q^{-s+1}=q^{-s-1}$. For $s=0$, no defect string intervenes: the two terminal resolutions give $\delta-q=q^{-1}$. The surviving matchings in this second branch are reflected versions of the first branch's matchings, but the coefficients just computed come from its own smoothing choices; reflection is linear and does not invert the scalar $q$. Every discarded resolution adds an arc and is zero in the quotient. Hence $F_m$ acts on $W_{m,s}$ as $q^{s+1}+q^{-s-1}$. [A1, F1, F2, F4, step 5.1, step 6.2, algebra]
 
